From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yan <Yan>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 23:09:18 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - async pathfinding: don't touch the regionized
 PathTypeCache off-region
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Soak caught it: every async path solve NPE'd at PathfindingContext.<init> ->
ServerLevel.getPathTypeCache() -> getCurrentWorldData().pathTypesByPosCache,
because getCurrentWorldData() (a region-thread thread-local) is null on the
AsyncPath worker. Solves failed and degraded to the stale path (no crash,
but async pathfinding was non-functional).

PathfindingContext now only uses the shared regionized cache when actually on
a region tick thread (TickRegionScheduler.getCurrentRegionizedWorldData() !=
null); off-region it falls back to no cache — getPathTypeFromState's static
computer is correct, just uncached for that one solve. On-region pathfinding
is unchanged (still cached).

diff --git a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathfindingContext.java b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathfindingContext.java
index 64e1a34de133beccb90486f247e7e74d6535941f..e01bb2b30552a6bb8f35d780e235cec6cb969fa6 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathfindingContext.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/world/level/pathfinder/PathfindingContext.java
@@ -15,7 +15,13 @@ public class PathfindingContext {
 
     public PathfindingContext(final CollisionGetter level, final Mob mob) {
         this.level = level;
-        if (mob.level() instanceof ServerLevel serverLevel) {
+        // SourbyCraft - async pathfinding: the regionized PathTypeCache lives on the CURRENT region's
+        // world data (ServerLevel.getPathTypeCache -> getCurrentWorldData().pathTypesByPosCache), which
+        // is null on the async-pathfinding worker thread (not a region tick thread). Only use the shared
+        // cache when actually running on a region thread; off-region, fall back to no cache — the static
+        // path-type computer in getPathTypeFromState is correct, just uncached for that one solve.
+        if (mob.level() instanceof ServerLevel serverLevel
+            && io.papermc.paper.threadedregions.TickRegionScheduler.getCurrentRegionizedWorldData() != null) {
             this.cache = serverLevel.getPathTypeCache();
         } else {
             this.cache = null;
